{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792490050,"nonce":"0a1AIAx0hMwplCBtv38GekKEo5A=","title":"Unmount command palette rows while closed","message":"The command center eagerly creates its file rows in a detached Floating panel even while closed. A 429-file workspace therefore retains all command items, labels, icons and inline-flow layout pieces at the no-tabs baseline. Tab document cleanup does not own these resources.\n\nBuild the palette body only when opened, release it on close, retain lightweight request/action metadata, and keep mode switching, picker selection, filter restoration, line navigation and rapid reopen functional. Own deferred focus hooks so body disposal removes pending callbacks. Verify detached identities and text registries, not only visible tree counts.\n\nAdopt upstream Ashui 3cb48b22375465fb8deca217f66bcac68f1eaf82, currently the latest available main, for its InlineFlow piece/box cleanup and breadcrumb regression. This retains the image-residency feature. Do not infer a universal per-element cost or promise a process-footprint reduction from node counts alone.","files":null}]}